Fixed. The bug was in `llm/llama_server.go`: both SSE stream parsers (completion at ~line 1506 and chat at ~line 1793) treated any non-empty line without a `data: ` prefix as a JSON event. SSE comment/ping lines like `: ping` therefore hit `json.Unmarshal` and errored out.

The fix skips comment lines per the SSE spec (any line starting with `:`):

```go
// SSE comment lines (e.g. ": ping" keepalives) must be ignored.
if line[0] == ':' {
    continue
}
```

added in both scanner loops. `go test -count=1 ./llm/...` passes and `go vet` is clean.
